{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x$ or any other non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x}{‖x‖\\,‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 5+5\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-1)}{\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{63}\\sqrt{27}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{3\\sqrt{7}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{7})≈{49.11}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338669 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338670 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338671 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338672 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338673 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1041 "selection" 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338671 13194139535227 true] [17592186338668 1110 #uuid "39a0d3e0-d366-5154-9582-ba12b2b89791" 13194139535227 true] [17592186338669 1034 "{56.22}^{∘}" 13194139535227 true] [17592186338669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535227 true] [17592186338669 1111 #uuid "8675bade-c9b3-540c-8993-c449bab62fe0" 13194139535227 true] [17592186338670 1034 "{40.20}^{∘}" 13194139535227 true] [17592186338670 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535227 true] 